{0 neodriver_eio}

The Eio backend of the driver: network transport, Bolt protocol and the
user-facing connection, session and transaction layers, in direct style
(OCaml 5).

- {!module:Neodriver_eio.Driver} — the entry point: [Driver.connect] builds a
  session from a URI and auth token.
- {!module:Neodriver_eio.Conn} — a minimal Bolt connection (connect,
  authenticate, RUN/PULL/DISCARD, transactions).
- {!module:Neodriver_eio.Session} — a per-session connection: auto-commit
  queries, explicit and managed transactions with retry.
- {!module:Neodriver_eio.Tx} — explicit transactions (BEGIN / COMMIT /
  ROLLBACK).
- {!module:Neodriver_eio.Neo4jResult} — a lazily-streamed query result
  (next / peek / fetch / consume / single).
- {!module:Neodriver_eio.Summary} — the summary of a query result (counters,
  plan, notifications).
- {!module:Neodriver_eio.Transport}, {!module:Neodriver_eio.Bolt},
  {!module:Neodriver_eio.State}, {!module:Neodriver_eio.Handshake} — the
  transport and protocol layers.

The root {!module:Neodriver_eio} aggregates all of the above.
